   "range_provenance": {
    "source_location": "Tables S2-S3; Seagle (2008) Table 1 and subsolidus supplement for Fe/FeO",
    "notes": "Marginal experimental coverage, not a rectangular phase-stability field. Fe/FeO upper bounds include earlier Seagle approximate isobars; new-study-only bounds and selected-row extrema are in the reproduction JSON. fcc Fe and stoichiometric B1 FeO must remain within their source phase/composition fields. The 295 K reference is an extrapolation. NiO is a source cubic-average B1 model across unresolved magnetic distortion."
   },
   "fit_datasets": [
    "feo_campbell_2009_table_s2_pvt",
    "feo_seagle_2008_supplement_volume_temperature"
   ],
   "notes": "Equation (5) and Table 1: 295 K BM3 plus Mie-Gruneisen-Debye, gamma=gamma0*(V/V0)^q and theta=theta0*(V/V0)^(-gamma(V)). No explicit electronic or anharmonic pressure. Source molar V0 is converted to the Z=4 conventional cell using exact SI Avogadro constant. Italicized Table 1 values are held fixed, and nonitalic values with errors are fitted. The confidence convention and covariance of published errors are not specified. Temperature-corrected workbook values are used as printed; no second correction is applied. The published fit also includes Seagle et al. (2008). Its 81 V-T rows are linked, but exact row-wise pressures and Campbell recalibration are not published. Independent refits therefore report a current-study subset and a nominal-isobar sensitivity reconstruction. Only stable fcc-Fe rows enter this branch; hcp Fe is explicitly adopted from Dewaele (2006), not a new Campbell fit. ",
   "pressure_calibration": {
    "status": "resolved",
    "audit_date": "2026-09-19",
    "methods": [
     {
      "kind": "equation_of_state",
      "material": "NaCl B1",
      "reference": {
       "authors": [
        "Decker"
       ],
       "year": 1971,
       "source": "Journal of Applied Physics",
       "volume": "42",
       "locator": "3239-3244",
       "doi": "10.1063/1.1660714"
      },
      "source_location": "Sections 2.1-2.2; Tables S2-S3, NaCl B1 rows"
     },
     {
      "kind": "equation_of_state",
      "material": "NaCl B2",
      "reference": {
       "authors": [
        "Fei",
        "Ricolleau",
        "Frank",
        "Mibe",
        "Shen",
        "Prakapenka"
       ],
       "year": 2007,
       "source": "PNAS",
       "volume": "104",
       "locator": "9182-9186",
       "doi": "10.1073/pnas.0609013104"
      },
      "source_location": "Section 2.2; Tables S2-S3, NaCl B2 rows"
     }
    ],
    "recalculation": {
     "status": "reference_eos_not_bundled",
     "notes": "Paired NaCl phase, molar volume, effective temperature and their errors are bundled for every current-study row. The exact Decker B1/Fei B2 pair is not registered as a complete executable catalog calibration route. Use the tabulated pressure; do not substitute a newer NaCl scale. Seagle fit-input rows have Fe volumes and temperatures but no NaCl readings or individual pressures."
    },
    "notes": "MAP detector angle calibrated with NaCl a=5.6402 A (JCPDS 05-0628); DAC geometry with CeO2. MAP cooling cycles minimize deviatoric stress. The article writes DAC T_sample=295+0.97*(T_meas-295) and T_NaCl=(3*T_meas+295)/4. The workbook uses a 293 K baseline for some Ni-NiO DAC runs and 295 K for others; preserve its stored values. Equation (4) prints sigma_TNaCl=(T_meas-295)/2, while the hot DAC workbook rows use (T_meas-T_ambient)/4; preserve the workbook uncertainties. The workbook pressure-threshold footnote is approximate: honor the explicit NaCl phase column, including B2 rows below 26 GPa."
   },
   "parameter_provenance": {
    "determination_method": "Measurements or their experimental reduction determine this EOS; source: Sections 2.1-2.2 and 3; Equation (5), Table 1, page 560; Official mmc1.pdf Figure S1 and mmc2.xls Tables S2-S5.",
    "equation": "Section 4.1 Equation (5), page 560, and its immediately following gamma(V) and theta(V) definitions. BM3 reference; FeO has K0_prime fixed to 4 (BM2-equivalent reference).",
    "V0": "Table 1: 7.076 cm3/mol, fixed from JCPDS, footnote a; source does not identify the card number. Conversion Vcell=Vmolar*Z*1e24/NA, Z=4. No source V0 error.",
    "K0": "Table 1, fitted; uncertainty as printed, confidence unspecified.",
    "K0_prime": "Table 1 fixed, footnote c: Funamori et al. (1996).",
    "thermal": {
     "Tr": "Equation (5): 295 K reference subtraction.",
     "theta0": "Table 1, fixed from Chase (1998), footnote e.",
     "gamma0": "Table 1, fitted; uncertainty as printed.",
     "q": "Table 1, fitted; uncertainty as printed.",
     "n": "Physical atoms per source molar formula: one for metal, two for monoxide; fixed Debye normalization."
    }
